{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe Lahn runs quiet under the evening sky. We have left the bustle of Giessen, where the professors’ hospitality was warm, though the wine perhaps a touch too generous for an evening walk. I parted ways with our Frankfurt-bound friends, glad to continue with Herr, the schoolteacher. He is a man of quiet intellect, and our conversation along the river bank was pleasant, if not entirely without the friction of differing views on the nature of the state.\n\nWe passed Weilburg, that old princely residence, standing silent against the hill. It strikes me as a monument to a time when freedom was the privilege of a few, rather than the substance of all. It is good to see the past recede behind us. I am tired, but my spirits are high. The journey is less about the destination and more about the movement itself. Keep the house warm. I shall write again from Frankfurt.\n\nYour devoted,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080129,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":201,"prompt_tokens":944,"total_tokens":1145,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-2NHmSMFDyIf6gMBvuI193UxUDpSlUTxp","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":944,"prompt_ms":908.785,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9626959745762712,"prompt_per_second":1038.7495392199476,"predicted_n":201,"predicted_ms":4773.365,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.866825,"predicted_per_second":41.89916337845524}}